@startuml
' MIGHTYCorgi - UC-03 Select a Corgi Class
' Based on docs/use_cases/UC-03_Corgi_Class_Selection.md
hide footbox
title UC-03 - Select a Corgi Class During Character Creation

actor Player
participant "Frontend\n(Character creation)" as FE
participant "Backend\n(Character service)" as BE
database "SQLite\n(Characters / classes)" as DB

' Basic flow: steps 1-2
Player -> FE : Start creating a new Corgi (1)
FE -> BE : Request available starter classes (2)
BE -> DB : Read class definitions and milestones

break [2a: Class definitions unavailable]
    DB --> BE : Class definitions could not be loaded
    BE --> FE : Report loading failure
    FE --> Player : Report problem; offer retry or cancellation
    alt [Player retries]
        Player -> FE : Retry loading class definitions
        ref over FE, DB : Return to step 2 - load class definitions
    else [Player cancels]
        Player -> FE : Cancel character creation
        FE -> FE : Discard new-character draft
    end
end

DB --> BE : Barkmage, S.P.A.W. Agent, Royal Barkguard
BE --> FE : Playstyles, starting features, later milestones,\nshared base abilities
FE --> Player : Show three classes and available information

' Basic flow: steps 3-4, plus alternative 3a
Player -> FE : Select one starter class (3)
FE --> Player : Preview chosen playstyle, base abilities,\nstarting and later locked features (4)

loop [3a: Player changes class before confirmation]
    Player -> FE : Choose another starter class
    FE --> Player : Update preview without creating a character
end

break [5a: Player cancels at step 5 or earlier]
    Player -> FE : Cancel character creation
    FE -> FE : Discard pending selection and character draft
    FE --> Player : No character created; existing Corgis unchanged
end

' Basic flow: steps 5-6
Player -> FE : Confirm selected class and required information (5)
FE -> BE : Create character(details, classId)
BE -> BE : Validate class availability and character information

break [6a: Class ID invalid or unavailable]
    BE --> FE : Reject invalid class; no character saved
    FE --> Player : Explain problem; reload valid classes
    ref over FE, DB : Return to step 2 - reload valid classes
end

break [6b: Character information missing or invalid]
    BE --> FE : Reject invalid information; no character saved
    FE --> Player : Explain corrections; keep selected class visible
    ref over Player, FE : Return to step 5 - correct and reconfirm
end

BE -> DB : Atomically create new Corgi for this player\nwith selected class, shared base abilities,\nstarting features and initial progression

break [6c: Persistence fails]
    DB --> BE : Storage failed; transaction rolled back
    BE --> FE : No partial character; existing Corgis unchanged
    FE --> Player : Report failure; offer retry or cancellation
    alt [Player retries]
        Player -> FE : Retry creating this character
        ref over Player, FE : Return to step 5 - reconfirm creation
    else [Player cancels]
        Player -> FE : Cancel character creation
        FE -> FE : Discard new-character draft
    end
end

' Basic flow: successful persistence is the normal continuation (steps 6-7)
DB --> BE : Committed (characterId, classId); old Corgis unchanged
BE --> FE : Creation successful; character available in roster
FE --> Player : Confirm creation; show new Corgi in roster (7)
@enduml
